## LoadOnDemand: 1

bootstrap.lua

# File list converted from the old options.xml include manifest.
# Order is load-bearing. ..\QUI\ paths load files from the main addon
# (parent-dir TOC entries are client-supported; Blizzard_PTRFeedbackGlue ships them).
#
# NOTE: LoadOnDemand — ~2.9 MB stays off the login path; the first options
# open pays the compile cost (QUI:EnsureOptionsLoaded, every open path routes
# through it). Login-time theme reads (accent color for layout mode, info bar,
# datatexts) are served by core/theme.lua, which pre-creates QUI.GUI; the
# framework merges into that table on load. The OptionalDeps above only order
# this addon after the login-class module addons when both load (their settings
# builders are loaded here); no builder captures a module symbol at file scope,
# so the ordering is belt-and-suspenders (proven by the headless generator
# smoke test).
search_synonyms.lua
# The generated search index, packed as a long-bracket string (~1.2 MB).
# Loading this file lexes ONE token; framework.lua compiles it on first search.
# It used to be the LoadOnDemand QUI_OptionsSearch addon — one folder for
# one deferral point. Packing gives the same deferral without the folder.
search_cache.lua
framework.lua
border_control.lua
reorder_list.lua
shared.lua
wizard.lua
# Options-only settings framework, deferred out of the login path. Every
# consumer reaches these lazily (inside a function) from UI-build code; none
# is captured at file scope on the login path. Loaded here ahead of the
# surfaces/pins/content files that use them. Order among the 9 is irrelevant
# (none cross-references another at file scope). The sibling framework files
# util/render_adapters/registry/schema/provider_features/pins/pins_lifecycle
# stay in QUI.toc — feature registration needs them at login.
..\QUI\core\settings\providers.lua
..\QUI\core\settings\provider_panels.lua
..\QUI\core\settings\model_kit.lua
..\QUI\core\settings\fields.lua
..\QUI\core\settings\surfaces.lua
..\QUI\core\settings\surface_features.lua
..\QUI\core\settings\nav.lua
..\QUI\core\settings\renderer.lua
